1
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,490
Welcome to the Watermill Inn.

2
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:11,290
Oh, Richard,

3
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:13,840
it's exactly as it was when we were married!

4
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:16,450
And when I got married.

5
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:19,160
Even the old patchwork quilt is the same!

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:22,100
My great-grandmother made that quilt

7
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,470
when Teddy Roosevelt was President.

8
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:26,890
In those days, when they made quilts.

9
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:31,080
they cut patches

10
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:33,440
so that each one would be a part of it.

11
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:34,910
What a lovely tradition!

12
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:36,860
Thank you for calling us.

13
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:40,790
I remember you and your wife

14
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:42,590
We were very young.

15
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:45,150
And very much in love.

16
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:46,820
We have a baby now.

17
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:50,380
How wonderful! A boy or a girl?

18
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:52,730
A boy--Max.

19
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:54,430
Do you have a picture?

20
00:00:54,430 --> 00:01:00,210
Would a professional photographer be without a picture?

21
00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:03,080
Oh, he's adorable!

22
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:04,360
And very bright.

23
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:06,480
Like his father. A real Stewart.

24
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:08,950
And very good-looking, like his mother.

25
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:11,160
Well, it's nice to have you with us again.

26
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:13,550
Next time, bring the baby.

27
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:15,720
You see, Richard? Max is welcome here.

28
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,550
Not on our anniversary.

29
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:20,200
This vacation is for you and me.

30
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:22,660
If there's anything you need, please call me.

31
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:27,160
I'll be in the front office all day.

32
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:35,780
Oh, I took the liberty of ordering some breakfast for you.

33
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:54,230
Just put it over there, Charles.

34
00:01:54,230 --> 00:01:57,380
Thank you, Charles.

35
00:01:57,380 --> 00:01:59,900
Compliments of the Watermill Inn.

36
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:00,540
Thank you.

37
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:05,800
Thank you so much.

38
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:09,610
Now, this is my idea of a good time.

39
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:16,970
Let's see ... hotcakes and maple syrup, with scrambled eggs.

40
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:20,810
Umm ... smell that coffee ... cinnamon and cloves.

41
00:02:20,810 --> 00:02:23,160
Homemade buttermilk biscuits.

42
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:26,750
Slices of orange with burnt honey.

43
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:28,400
Let's eat!

44
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,500
First I want to call home

45
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,310
and check on your mother and the baby.

46
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:32,680
Honey, if there were any problems,

47
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:34,070
she would call us.

48
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:36,260
She doesn't know we've changed hotels.

49
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:46,080
You're right. Of course.

50
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:48,270
Hello, operator.

51
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:56,920
I'd like to call Riverdale, New York.

52
00:02:56,920 --> 00:03:00,410
This food is heavenly, isn't it?

53
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:11,470
This whole place is heavenly.

54
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:14,910
Do you remember that old desk?

55
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:17,420
Mrs. Montefiore told me that

56
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:18,870
George Washington sat at that desk

57
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:21,660
and wrote to his wife Martha.

58
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:24,360
What do you want to do after breakfast?

59
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:27,010
Why don't we take a walk down to the river?

60
00:03:27,010 --> 00:03:28,260
In the rain?

61
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:36,610
No. Look out the window. The sun is shining!

62
00:03:36,610 --> 00:03:39,610
Now this is my idea of a good time!
